Package: flippies-boot
Version: 1.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Create Flippies <flippies@deb.flip>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: flipboot boot area tools for the Create Flippies PC
 The Create Flippies PC boots Linux through flipboot (stage 1 in the MBR, stage 2 in
 sectors 1 to 127), which loads the kernel from one of two slots in the boot area
 partition. flipboot-update writes a new kernel into the inactive slot, checks it and
 makes it the active slot. A kernel postinst.d hook runs it for every installed kernel.
